WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Welcome to The First Overnight Shift. This short lesson covers your arrival, the quiet hours, and the morning handoff.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Three moments shape a calm overnight shift: the arrival conversation, the quiet hours, and the morning handoff.

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Before the parents go to bed, confirm the feeding plan: what the baby takes, how much, and when.

4
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Agree on exactly when and how to wake the parents, so you never have to guess in the middle of the night.

5
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Keep a shift log of every feed, every diaper, each sleep stretch, and anything that stands out.

6
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:06.000
For every sleep: on the back, on a firm flat surface, with nothing loose in the sleep space.

7
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:16.000
If something concerns you, follow the wake instructions you agreed on. In an emergency, call 911 first.

8
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:28.000
In the morning, give a short handoff: feeds, diapers, sleep, anything unusual, and supplies running low.

9
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Download the First Shift Checklist, then take the five question quiz. Score four out of five to earn your certificate.
